messages:
mila: Heads-up: onboarding tickets keep coming in where the JS quickstart shows `Error: Bad request` and no hint. Python/Go are giving a structured code + hint. Can we decide the short-term fix?
dan: Ugh. Thats a brutal first-run experience. Quick plan: make JS throw typed Error subclasses and update quickstart.
rik: Agreed. Current JS unwraps `body.message || statusText`. We should parse canonical envelope if present: `{code, human_message, hint, retry_after, http_status}`. If absent, synthesize one from status + message.
jess: Streaming edge-case: many streaming responses close with just a status. Two options: 1) set `x-rw-error: 1` and include a final NDJSON line with the envelope; 2) include a compact header `x-rw-err-json` with base64(payload). Prefer 1) for readability. SDKs must fall back to status->code mapping.
mila: For quickstart copy let's show `instanceof` and a `code` check fallback. Short example we can paste:```
try {
  await client.chat.completions.create(payload)
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof InvalidArgumentError || err.code === 'InvalidArgument') {
    ui.show(err.human_message || 'Your prompt is too long')
  } else if (err instanceof RateLimitError) {
    scheduleRetry(err.retry_after || 60)
  } else {
    console.error(err)
  }
}
```
dan: Mapping table proposal in docs (canonical codes): 400=InvalidArgument, 401=AuthenticationFailed, 403=PermissionDenied, 404=NotFound, 409=Conflict, 422=InvalidState, 429=RateLimit, 5xx=ServerError. Docs should explicitly say `RateLimit` includes `retry_after (seconds)` when present.
rik: Addendum: human_message must be short and non-technical. Examples: 'prompt exceeds 8k tokens; try shortening' not stack dumps. Enforce in server RFC.
jess: I'll update sampleapp quickstart tonight to use the new snippet and stop recommending `err.type` checks. Also add a tiny smoke test that POSTs an oversized prompt and asserts `err.code === 'InvalidArgument'`.
mila: I'll own doc changes and a small note about streaming trailers.
dan: I'll take the JS SDK change (Error subclasses, compat shim for old `message` response). Plan: add classes InvalidArgumentError, RateLimitError, ServerError, and include properties `code,human_message,hint,retry_after,http_status`. Add tests. ETA: PR by tomorrow.
docbot: Created issue INFER-2026 "sdk-js: error subclasses + quickstart parity" assigned to dan. https://github.com/redwood/sdk-js/issues/2026
mila: After PRs merge, CS will validate the open tickets. Also set a deprecation note: compatibility shim for legacy `message` bodies kept for 1 major release.
rik: Tiny follow-up: add a linter in js-sdk that fails if `new RedwoodError` is created without `code` and `human_message` fields.
mila: Solid. Timeline: quickstart + sampleapp tonight, JS SDK PR tomorrow, docs by Friday. I'll notify CS. Thanks all.
jess: :thumbsup:
